commit b680d2637730d230f753bcb79610592864d2ed54

C03: the screen excerpt travels as a list of lines and the grounding check ignores JSON escapes (SCREEN1421)

SCREEN1419 measured the screen-content questions on the masked failure lenses: the Spanish forms published faithful readings, but the two English variants published nothing. Their drafts quoted the three excerpt lines in a single quotation copying the JSON newline escapes of seen.text, and _ocr_unsupported_terms took the glued fragments (the escape letter stuck to the next word) as words foreign to the recognized text.

llm._compose_situation_payload: the ocr.read projection carries the excerpt as seen.lines (a list) next to seen.text, and the screen-reading instruction asks for each line in its own quotation marks.
llm._ocr_unsupported_terms: literal \n, \r and \t escapes in the draft are separators before tokenizing; «visu» joins the framing stems (the honest preface says it cannot visualize images).

Offline probe on the SCREEN1419 private audit: the 18 vetoed drafts pass every veto now; an invented description is still vetoed as ocr_unsupported_terms. Mind only, no App recompilation. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


